  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Les jeunes ont leur mot &#xe0; dire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to promote  youth participation in the management of local affairs through revival  of the communal infrastructure(Library jnan lward )by making it a space  of cooperation, dialogue and creativity and for an active and influential citizenship ofyouth in local decision-making.  It aims to mobilize young people and  CSOs  to sign a petition for the opening of the municipal library Jnan Lward  to youth and improve  its services . Finally an action plan  will be developed  with participatory approach for the animation of this space.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association Citoyen De Rue</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Founded in 2010 in Fez, Citoyen De Rue is a Moroccan non-profit organization committed to institutionalizing youth participation atlocal and regional levels.
It works to promote their civil, political, economic, social, and cultural rights, placing young people at the heart of social and democratic change. Its mission is to contribute to the development of a democratic, just, and open Moroccan society, where every young person&#x2014;female or male, child or adult&#x2014;can express themselves, create, and actively contribute to building a collective future based on citizenship, responsibility, and dignity.
The organization adopts participatory and inclusive approaches based on peer education, artistic expression, advocacy, and gender equality.Vision: For a citizenaction that is modern, democratic, constructive, and participatory.The main areas of activity of Citoyen De Rue include:
- Civic participation, local governance,and participatory democracy
- Youth action and human rights
-Local public policiesChild protection a
-And gender equalityCultural and artistic exchanges</narrative>
  </participating-org>
